%U A398674 7715969649141617,207725665249898585,5906249991511577997,176844723805586366009,5561633570015615775865
%N A398674 Number of disconnected quasi-cubic graphs on 2*n + 1 vertices.
%C A398674 A quasi-cubic graph is a simple graph with one vertex of degree 4 and every other vertex of degree 3. By the handshaking lemma, it has odd order.
%C A398674 Let A_3(N), C_3(N), and R_3(N) count all quasi-cubic graphs, connected quasi-cubic graphs, and all cubic graphs on N vertices, respectively, with R_3(0) = 1. Unique component decomposition gives A_3(N) = Sum_j C_3(j)*R_3(N-j), and hence A_3(N)-C_3(N) = Sum_{j<N} C_3(j)*R_3(N-j).
%H A398674 Eric W. Weisstein, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Quasi-CubicGraph.html">Quasi-Cubic Graph</a>, MathWorld.
%F A398674 a(n) = A398638(n) - A398639(n). Also, a(n) = Sum_{j<2*n+1} C_3(j)*R_3(2*n+1-j).
%F A398674 G.f.: B(x)*(1 - 1/C(x)) where B(x) is the g.f. of A398638 and C(x) is the g.f. of A005638. - _Andrew Howroyd_, Aug 17 2026
%e A398674 a(12) = 80333985 = 1*516344 + 4*42110 + 27*4207 + 208*540 + 1958*94 + 21879*21 + 284331*6 + 4190340*2 + 68693115*1.
%Y A398674 Cf. A398638 (all quasi-cubic graphs), A398639 (connected quasi-cubic graphs), and A005638 (cubic graphs).
%K A398674 nonn
